    "title": "Apple Reportedly Exploring a Screenless Fitness Tracker to Take on Whoop - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jesse Hollington ,\n1 days ago Apple may be preparing to concede that even its most affordable Apple Watch SE is a bit pricey for anyone who just wants a basic health and fitness tracker. For years, the Apple Watch has been somewhat undercut by the likes of Google’s Fitbit, which offer a versatile range of fitness bands for well under $150. Some of them even come with basic screens to let you tell the time. Read full article",
